title: x4
---

set heading(numbering: none)

`x4` · repeat · fourth order.

# Form

`x.x4` on a symbol, `(a + b).x4` on a group. A recipe has one base and up to three operations.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `integral.x4` | $integral.x4$ | built and cached |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | Fourth order. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | Use a `sym` to give a recipe a short name. |
| Construction | Copies of the base side by side. A font glyph is used when one exists, for example two integrals. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- More than three operations on one base gives a warning.

# From LaTeX

`\iiiint` becomes `integral.x4`.

